### Underload Demo (CMK)
<hr style="width:100%;border-bottom:3px solid black;">

With the vanilla-Makefile version out of the way, here's a version showing off more of the 
[CMK-lang]({{mkdocs.site_relative_url}}/compiler) primitives.  A few things to highlight about that:

**Single-sourcing / Imports:** we keep things DRY by pulling in shared components that we don't plan to change, i.e. pulling in shared definitions from the Makefile twin in the last section. See also the documentation for:

* [`mk.import.def`]({{mkdocs.site_relative_url}}/macros)
* [`mk.import.target`]({{mkdocs.site_relative_url}}/macros)

**Triple-Quoted Inlines:** Are a form that CMK supports, with and without interpolation.
See also the documentation [here]({{mkdocs.site_relative_url}}/compiler/#triple-quote-literals).

**Callable Targets:** The `underload` VM reads its program from stdin, so the demos invoke
it with the callable-target sugar `this.underload("""...""")` (which lowers to
`"""...""" | this.underload`).  See also the documentation
[here]({{mkdocs.site_relative_url}}/compiler/#callable-targets).

